# Load-bearing rules for security:security-scan.
# This skill builds a shell command from user input and shells out to a
# third-party npm package, so its parsing and honesty rules are the ones that
# matter. CLI reference material lives in references/ and is not asserted here.

the external dependency is declared as not bundled :: [Ee]xternal dependency
a failed download or tool run is reported, not improvised around :: do not improvise|could not run
never interpolate $ARGUMENTS into the command :: never interpolate
a bare path becomes --path :: bare path.*--path|--path "<path>"
a non-existent path stops rather than falling back to the cwd :: never fall back to the current directory
--min-severity accepts only low, medium, high :: low.*medium.*high
an empty argument scans the current project's .claude :: [Ee]mpty.*scan
shell metacharacters stop the run :: metacharacters
unrecognized flags and extra positionals stop the run :: unrecognized flags
never guess at an unmatched argument :: Never guess
report what the command actually returned :: what the command actually returned
never claim a scan was filtered or scoped when the flag was not applied :: never describe a scan as filtered|Never describe a scan as filtered
